================================================================================
WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES
================================================================================

  One arm of the AAP-ANCHORED pair of the controlled A/B the AAP mandates
  (0.5.1, 0.9.1): the pinned tainted-sql-string rule from the pinned Opengrep
  ruleset, run over the subject the AAP names by path,
  core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/storage/DiskStore.scala, with taint
  analysis as the SOLE analysis difference between the two arms. It carries
  this arm's exact command, its argv delta against its sibling, the scan root
  and the pinned HEAD it ran against, the engine, rule and ruleset identities
  it ran under, its exit code, its wall time, the findings it produced with
  every line and every dataflow trace step, and the output's byte size and
  sha256 measured from the file on disk after the write.

  This is where the AAP-named subject's arms live, and this pair exists to
  report that subject's anchored expectation honestly rather than to satisfy
  it. Its verdict is below: the anchor is UNMET, with the mechanism measured
  rather than guessed, and the capability question is answered instead by the
  pair named in the CROSS-REFERENCE section.

================================================================================
WHY THIS FILE IS UNDER logs/ AND NEVER UNDER raw/
================================================================================

  Two independent reasons, either sufficient (AAP 0.5.1, 0.6.1). First, raw/
  is RUNNER-ONLY: it receives exactly one artifact per tool that writes one
  and nothing else, ever, so an A/B SARIF landing there would overwrite the
  opengrep.sarif the Stage 3 runner writes and the dataset would then be built
  from an A/B over ONE file instead of a scan over the whole scope. Second,
  this is one of the run's two deliberate second appearances: Opengrep appears
  here as the taint A/B subject and again as one of the nine scanned runners;
  Joern appears as a runner and again as the capability probe's subject. Each
  second appearance writes outside raw/ and contributes NO dataset row (AAP
  0.3.2).

