  session ran with the rule's pattern-sources replaced by a marker call that
  appears nowhere in the pinned tree (sinks and sanitizers untouched) returned
  0 findings on this same file, which is what a taint-derived result looks
  like when its source is removed. The line-72 finding IS produced by taint
  reachability. The reason it survives the A/B unchanged is that its flow is
  intraprocedural and the engine has no taint-off switch, not that a pattern
  matched it. That control is not an arm of the A/B - it differs from the
  pinned rule in the RULE rather than in the taint setting, so it corroborates
