================================================================================
APPENDIX E - mechanism control: the line-72 result is taint-derived
================================================================================

  Why this control exists. The two arms of this pair are byte-identical, so on
  their own they cannot show WHY the line-72 result survives the flag change -
  and the distinction decides what a reader should conclude. If the result
  were a bare pattern match, it would say nothing about taint at all; if it is
  taint reachability that the engine's default intraprocedural analysis
  already resolves, then the unmet anchor is a property of the SUBJECT rather
  than of the engine. This control settles that, and it settles it on the
  AAP-named subject itself.

